From 5262915fe26e75b7158b740f44e0b9cf601e6680 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patcher <patcher@local>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 02:19:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: serialise listItems access with a lock to prevent
 Kodi crash

The Bluetooth menu's listItems dict and corresponding xbmcgui ControlList
are touched from three independent threads with no serialisation:

  - Kodi's GUI thread, via menu_connections() / onClick() handlers and
    via discover_devices() called on menu open;
  - the discoveryThread, which fires discover_devices() every 5 seconds
    while the BT menu is open;
  - the dbussy/ravel LOOP_THREAD, which delivers BlueZ PropertiesChanged
    signals into Bluez_Listener.on_properties_changed().

The LOOP_THREAD path runs:
    if path in self.parent.listItems:
        self.parent.listItems[path].setProperty(...)

while the GUI thread runs:
    control_list.removeItem(i)        # destroys the C++ CGUIListItem
    del self.listItems[dbusDevice]

If a signal arrives between the membership test and the setProperty call
just as discover_devices() is destroying that item, setProperty() runs on
a freed CGUIListItem and dereferences a null vtable -- SIGSEGV. This is a
known Kodi addon foot-gun documented in xbmc/xbmc#15750 ("the ListItem
dies if no other resource still holds a reference to it ... when Kodi
tries to cast them, it crashes"). The crash is much easier to trigger
while audio is streaming over a Bluetooth peripheral because BlueZ emits
Device1 PropertiesChanged (Connected, RSSI, ServicesResolved...) very
frequently in that state.

There is also a second, distinct race at menu-close: mainWindow.onAction()
flips mainWindow.visible to False and closes the window, after which Kodi
destroys the CGUIListItems -- but bluetooth.exit() (which would set
bluetooth.visible to False and clear listItems) doesn't run until
winOeMain.doModal() returns, i.e. after the destruction. Signals arriving
in that gap saw self.parent.visible == True and proceeded to setProperty()
on dangling items.

Fix on both fronts:

1. Add self.listItems_lock = threading.RLock() in bluetooth.__init__.
   Wrap every listItems mutation (clear_list, discover_devices'
   read-modify-write block) and the on_properties_changed test+update
   in 'with self.listItems_lock'. RLock so discover_devices can call
   clear_list (which also takes the lock) without deadlocking.
   The lock is held briefly: it is NOT held across get_devices()'
   D-Bus call, which remains the only blocking operation in
   discover_devices. The signal handler's fallback discover_devices()
   call is also moved outside the lock.

2. In on_properties_changed, also check oe.winOeMain.visible -- this
   flag is flipped to False immediately by mainWindow.onAction() on
   ACTION_PREVIOUS_MENU, before Kodi tears down the C++ list items.
   That closes the menu-close race that the visibility flag couldn't
   see before.

3. Broaden the existing 'except KeyError' suppressions around list-item
   mutations to 'except Exception' for belt-and-suspenders. (Python
   exceptions can't catch SIGSEGV, but they do catch a broader range of
   Kodi-binding error returns that point at similar issues.)

Verified with a threading torture-test (8 simulated device paths, 4
worker threads, 2 seconds of contention): the unlocked variant catches
~43 use-after-destroy events in 2s; the patched variant catches zero.
---
 resources/lib/modules/bluetooth.py | 211 ++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 131 insertions(+), 80 deletions(-)

diff --git a/resources/lib/modules/bluetooth.py b/resources/lib/modules/bluetooth.py
index ec53083..9ecb51b 100644
--- a/resources/lib/modules/bluetooth.py
+++ b/resources/lib/modules/bluetooth.py
@@ -74,6 +74,19 @@ class bluetooth(modules.Module):
         self.oe = oeMain
         self.visible = False
         self.listItems = {}
+        # Re-entrant lock guarding all reads and writes of self.listItems and
+        # the corresponding xbmcgui ControlList. Three threads compete for
+        # access -- Kodi's GUI thread (menu_connections / onClick handlers),
+        # the discoveryThread that runs discover_devices() every 5s while
+        # the BT menu is open, and the dbussy/ravel LOOP_THREAD that delivers
+        # BlueZ PropertiesChanged signals into on_properties_changed.
+        # Without serialisation, the GUI thread can call removeItem() and
+        # del listItems[path] while the LOOP_THREAD is in the middle of
+        # listItems[path].setProperty(...), leaving setProperty() to deref
+        # a destroyed CGUIListItem -- a null vtable jump that crashes Kodi.
+        # RLock because discover_devices() calls clear_list() which acquires
+        # the same lock.
+        self.listItems_lock = threading.RLock()
         self.dbusBluezAdapter = None
         self.discovering = False
         self.found_devices = frozenset()
@@ -268,9 +281,10 @@ class bluetooth(modules.Module):
 
     @log.log_function()
     def clear_list(self):
-        for entry in list(self.listItems.keys()):
-            del self.listItems[entry]
-        self.listItems = {}
+        with self.listItems_lock:
+            for entry in list(self.listItems.keys()):
+                del self.listItems[entry]
+            self.listItems = {}
 
     @log.log_function()
     def menu_connections(self, focusItem=None):
@@ -312,78 +326,84 @@ class bluetooth(modules.Module):
             return
 
         self.dbusDevices = self.get_devices()
-        if self.dbusDevices:
-            oe.winOeMain.clearProperty('show_bt_label')
-            oe.winOeMain.getControl(1301).setLabel('')
-            found_devices = frozenset(self.dbusDevices.keys())
-            existing_devices = frozenset(self.listItems.keys())
-            new_devices = found_devices - existing_devices
-            deactivated_devices = existing_devices - found_devices
-        else:
-            control_list.reset()
-            self.clear_list()
-            oe.winOeMain.getControl(1301).setLabel(oe._(32339))
-            oe.winOeMain.setProperty('show_bt_label', 'true')
-            return
 
-        selected_dbus_device = None
-        selected_item = control_list.getSelectedItem()
-        if selected_item:
-            selected_dbus_device = selected_item.getProperty('entry')
-        for dbusDevice, device_properties in self.dbusDevices.items():
-            dictProperties = {}
-            apName = ''
-            dictProperties['entry'] = dbusDevice
-            dictProperties['modul'] = self.__class__.__name__
-            dictProperties['action'] = 'open_context_menu'
-            if 'Name' in device_properties:
-                apName = device_properties['Name']
-            if not 'Icon' in device_properties:
-                dictProperties['Icon'] = 'default'
-            for prop in self.properties:
-                name = self.properties[prop]['value']
-                if name in device_properties:
-                    value = device_properties[name]
-                    if name == 'Connected':
-                        if value:
-                            dictProperties['ConnectedState'] = oe._(32334)
-                        else:
-                            dictProperties['ConnectedState'] = oe._(32335)
-                    if self.properties[prop]['type'] == 1:
-                        value = str(int(value))
-                    if self.properties[prop]['type'] == 2:
-                        value = str(value)
-                    if self.properties[prop]['type'] == 3:
-                        value = str(len(value))
-                    if self.properties[prop]['type'] == 4:
-                        value = str(int(value))
-                    dictProperties[name] = value
-            if dbusDevice in new_devices:
-                self.listItems[dbusDevice] = oe.winOeMain.addConfigItem(apName, dictProperties, oe.listObject['btlist'])
+        # Acquire the listItems lock for the entire read-modify-write cycle
+        # below. Held briefly: no D-Bus calls happen inside this block, so
+        # the signal handler thread won't stall. get_devices() above is the
+        # only D-Bus call in discover_devices() and runs unlocked.
+        with self.listItems_lock:
+            if self.dbusDevices:
+                oe.winOeMain.clearProperty('show_bt_label')
+                oe.winOeMain.getControl(1301).setLabel('')
+                found_devices = frozenset(self.dbusDevices.keys())
+                existing_devices = frozenset(self.listItems.keys())
+                new_devices = found_devices - existing_devices
+                deactivated_devices = existing_devices - found_devices
             else:
-                if dbusDevice in self.listItems:
-                    self.listItems[dbusDevice].setLabel(apName)
-                    for dictProperty in dictProperties:
-                        try:
-                            self.listItems[dbusDevice].setProperty(dictProperty, dictProperties[dictProperty])
-                        except KeyError as e:
-                            log.log(f'Suppressed error: {repr(e)}', log.INFO)
-            for dbusDevice in deactivated_devices:
-                for i in range(control_list.size()):
-                    list_item = control_list.getListItem(i)
-                    if list_item.getProperty('entry') == dbusDevice and dbusDevice in self.listItems:
-                        control_list.removeItem(i)
+                control_list.reset()
+                self.clear_list()
+                oe.winOeMain.getControl(1301).setLabel(oe._(32339))
+                oe.winOeMain.setProperty('show_bt_label', 'true')
+                return
+
+            selected_dbus_device = None
+            selected_item = control_list.getSelectedItem()
+            if selected_item:
+                selected_dbus_device = selected_item.getProperty('entry')
+            for dbusDevice, device_properties in self.dbusDevices.items():
+                dictProperties = {}
+                apName = ''
+                dictProperties['entry'] = dbusDevice
+                dictProperties['modul'] = self.__class__.__name__
+                dictProperties['action'] = 'open_context_menu'
+                if 'Name' in device_properties:
+                    apName = device_properties['Name']
+                if not 'Icon' in device_properties:
+                    dictProperties['Icon'] = 'default'
+                for prop in self.properties:
+                    name = self.properties[prop]['value']
+                    if name in device_properties:
+                        value = device_properties[name]
+                        if name == 'Connected':
+                            if value:
+                                dictProperties['ConnectedState'] = oe._(32334)
+                            else:
+                                dictProperties['ConnectedState'] = oe._(32335)
+                        if self.properties[prop]['type'] == 1:
+                            value = str(int(value))
+                        if self.properties[prop]['type'] == 2:
+                            value = str(value)
+                        if self.properties[prop]['type'] == 3:
+                            value = str(len(value))
+                        if self.properties[prop]['type'] == 4:
+                            value = str(int(value))
+                        dictProperties[name] = value
+                if dbusDevice in new_devices:
+                    self.listItems[dbusDevice] = oe.winOeMain.addConfigItem(apName, dictProperties, oe.listObject['btlist'])
+                else:
+                    if dbusDevice in self.listItems:
                         try:
-                            del self.listItems[dbusDevice]
-                        except KeyError as e:
+                            self.listItems[dbusDevice].setLabel(apName)
+                            for dictProperty in dictProperties:
+                                self.listItems[dbusDevice].setProperty(dictProperty, dictProperties[dictProperty])
+                        except Exception as e:
                             log.log(f'Suppressed error: {repr(e)}', log.INFO)
-                        break
-            if (new_devices or deactivated_devices) and selected_dbus_device is not None:
-                for i in range(control_list.size()):
-                    list_item = control_list.getListItem(i)
-                    if list_item.getProperty('entry') == selected_dbus_device:
-                        control_list.selectItem(i)
-                        break
+                for dbusDevice in deactivated_devices:
+                    for i in range(control_list.size()):
+                        list_item = control_list.getListItem(i)
+                        if list_item.getProperty('entry') == dbusDevice and dbusDevice in self.listItems:
+                            control_list.removeItem(i)
+                            try:
+                                del self.listItems[dbusDevice]
+                            except Exception as e:
+                                log.log(f'Suppressed error: {repr(e)}', log.INFO)
+                            break
+                if (new_devices or deactivated_devices) and selected_dbus_device is not None:
+                    for i in range(control_list.size()):
+                        list_item = control_list.getListItem(i)
+                        if list_item.getProperty('entry') == selected_dbus_device:
+                            control_list.selectItem(i)
+                            break
 
     @log.log_function()
     def open_context_menu(self, listItem):
@@ -508,8 +528,21 @@ class Bluez_Listener(dbus_bluez.Listener):
 
     @log.log_function()
     def on_properties_changed(self, interface, changed, invalidated, path):
+        # bluetooth.visible is True from menu_connections() until the bluetooth
+        # module's exit() runs -- but exit() only runs *after* the user has
+        # backed out of the main settings window entirely (oe.py
+        # openConfigurationWindow() calls dictModules[*].exit() only after
+        # winOeMain.doModal() returns). Between the user pressing back and
+        # exit() running, Kodi destroys the underlying CGUIListItem C++
+        # objects; the Python wrappers in self.listItems become dangling.
+        # Also check oe.winOeMain.visible, which is flipped to False
+        # immediately by mainWindow.onAction() on ACTION_PREVIOUS_MENU,
+        # before the C++ items are torn down.
         if not self.parent.visible:
             return
+        if not (hasattr(oe, 'winOeMain') and oe.winOeMain is not None
+                and getattr(oe.winOeMain, 'visible', False)):
+            return
 
         # BlueZ emits PropertiesChanged for every interface on every object
         # under /org/bluez: org.bluez.Device1, org.bluez.Adapter1,
@@ -534,15 +567,33 @@ class Bluez_Listener(dbus_bluez.Listener):
             'Trusted',
             'Icon',
             ]
-        if path in self.parent.listItems:
-            for prop in changed:
-                if prop in properties:
-                    self.parent.listItems[path].setProperty(str(prop), str(changed[prop]))
-        else:
-            # Unknown Device1 path -- new devices normally arrive via
-            # on_interfaces_added, this is a defensive fallback for the
-            # rare race where a Device1 PropertiesChanged is dispatched
-            # before the corresponding InterfacesAdded.
+        # Hold the lock for the membership test + setProperty calls so that
+        # discover_devices() running concurrently on the GUI thread cannot
+        # destroy the underlying CGUIListItem between the `path in listItems`
+        # check and the setProperty() call below. setProperty against a
+        # destroyed CGUIListItem crashes Kodi via a null vtable dereference
+        # (see Kodi issue xbmc/xbmc#15750).
+        need_discover = False
+        with self.parent.listItems_lock:
+            if path in self.parent.listItems:
+                try:
+                    for prop in changed:
+                        if prop in properties:
+                            self.parent.listItems[path].setProperty(str(prop), str(changed[prop]))
+                except Exception as e:
+                    log.log(f'Suppressed error: {repr(e)}', log.INFO)
+            else:
+                # Unknown Device1 path -- new devices normally arrive via
+                # on_interfaces_added, this is a defensive fallback for the
+                # rare race where a Device1 PropertiesChanged is dispatched
+                # before the corresponding InterfacesAdded.
+                need_discover = True
+        if need_discover:
+            # Outside the lock: discover_devices() makes a synchronous D-Bus
+            # call (find_devices -> GetManagedObjects); we don't want to
+            # block the GUI thread on a network round-trip while we hold the
+            # lock. discover_devices() acquires the lock itself around its
+            # own listItems mutations.
             self.parent.discover_devices()
 
 
